From 795119b0277d8f3b88ca8b7606e1aa8cbb798d39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc <marc@schuetze.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:15:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] q800: allow byte and word reads of the CPU ID register

The machine ID register at 0x5ffffffc only accepts 32-bit accesses.
The Mac ROM with checksum FF7439EE (LC 475 / Quadra 605 / LC 575),
whose machine table also contains the Quadra 800 entry (CPU ID
0x2bad), reads the register with a 16-bit access late in its startup
tests:

    cmpi.w #0x2bad,0x5ffffffc

QEMU raises an access fault for it, the ROM records a POST failure and
ends up polling the SCC receive status with interrupts masked forever:
grey screen, no chime.

Accept 1 to 4 byte reads and return the addressed bytes of the
big-endian register, as a 68040 partial read of a 32-bit register
would see them (a word read at offset 0 returns 0xa55a, so the
comparison above is false and the ROM carries on). Writes remain
ignored.

With this change that ROM boots System 7.5.3 to the Finder on the q800
machine.
---
 hw/m68k/q800.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/m68k/q800.c b/hw/m68k/q800.c
index 5d0cb4d483..75c150e6b0 100644
--- a/hw/m68k/q800.c
+++ b/hw/m68k/q800.c
@@ -205,7 +205,8 @@ static const MemoryRegionOps macio_alias_ops = {
 
 static uint64_t machine_id_read(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, unsigned size)
 {
-    return Q800_MACHINE_ID;
+    /* Big-endian register: offset 0 holds the most significant byte */
+    return extract32(Q800_MACHINE_ID, (4 - addr - size) * 8, size * 8);
 }
 
 static void machine_id_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, uint64_t val,
@@ -218,7 +219,7 @@ static const MemoryRegionOps machine_id_ops = {
     .write = machine_id_write,
     .endianness = DEVICE_BIG_ENDIAN,
     .valid = {
-        .min_access_size = 4,
+        .min_access_size = 1,
         .max_access_size = 4,
     },
 };
